  - FIXED:   Security issues across HTTPD and management paths, including
             stronger administrator session tokens, protected login state,
             authenticated CGI CSRF checks, WebUI XSS fixes, and safer
             firmware-upgrade staging and credential handling.
  - FIXED:   Bounds, overflow, race, and reference-lifetime defects across
             kernel networking and storage, including IPv6, PPP/PPPoE,
             netfilter/conntrack/CTF, filesystem metadata, and USB handling.
  - CHANGED: Hardened build settings for network-facing daemons with stack
             protection, format checks, and RELRO/NOW linker options; added
             bounds checks for oversized socket-send buffers.
  - ADDED:   IPsec client support in VPN Director, including selective
             per-client routing through IPsec tunnels.
  - CHANGED: Dynamic Routing can display both the main routing table and
             IPsec table 220 while an IPsec client tunnel is active.
  - FIXED:   VPN Status now correctly reports IPsec tunnel information and
             refreshes; restored IPsec routing rules after WAN changes.
  - ADDED:   DNSCrypt settings on the Ethernet WAN page.
  - ADDED:   Firmware update checks against GitHub ion releases for the DSL-AC68U.
  - FIXED:   DNS Director per-client IPv4 filtering, which had been
             effectively broken since its introduction: DHCP now advertises
             each client's selected DNS server, and applying changes refreshes
             the firewall and dnsmasq configuration.
  - CHANGED: FRR WebUI status and configuration now use native FRR sockets
             and configuration-backed settings, with FRR_CONFIG_DIR support;
             refreshed the Advanced VPN Client page and routing-page layout.
  - CHANGED: WebUI switch controls now use shared CSS toggles instead of
             legacy switch plugins.
  - CHANGED: Stop logging acsd (Auto Channel Selection Daemon)
             activity to syslog by default.         
  - UPDATED: OpenSSL to 1.1.1zh, OpenVPN to 2.7.9, strongSwan to 6.1.0,
             curl to 8.23.0, BusyBox to 1.36.1, dnscrypt-proxy to 2.1.20,
             and haveged to 1.9.27.



